Subject: [PATCH] mtk: mt_wifi: dump the MacTable once when read without argument

Backport of MedyMa/immortalwrt-mt798x-6.6 0f3af09 ("mt_hwifi: log the
MacTable dump once instead of on every poll").

The proc/driver/mac_table read with an empty argument dumps every entry
of every BSS on each poll, so a userspace poller floods the log. Return
the cached result after the first dump; explicit arguments (e.g. "sta")
still walk the table.

--- a/mt_wifi/embedded/common/cmm_info.c
+++ b/mt_wifi/embedded/common/cmm_info.c
@@ -11609,7 +11609,15 @@
 	CHAR *pch = NULL;
 	UINT32 check_aid = 0;
 	UINT32 check_bssidx = 0;
+	static BOOLEAN mac_table_dumped = FALSE;
+	BOOLEAN one_shot;
+
+	one_shot = (arg == NULL || strlen(arg) == 0);
+	if (one_shot && mac_table_dumped)
+		return TRUE;
+	if (one_shot)
+		mac_table_dumped = TRUE;
 
 	MTWF_PRINT("%s(): arg=%s\n", __func__, (arg == NULL ? "" : arg));
 
 	if (arg && strlen(arg)) {
